{
  "_doc": "Per-locale pronunciation overrides for the Kokoro TTS engine. When a term in this dictionary appears in a chunk, the renderer wraps it with an espeak-phonemizer hint so the synthesized audio says it correctly. Terms NOT in this dictionary use Kokoro's default pronunciation (which is generally good but routinely mangles brand names, neighborhood names, and acronyms).",
  "_format": "Each locale section maps source_term → { say-as | ipa | espeak | spell }. Use 'spell' for acronyms read letter-by-letter. Use 'ipa' for the strictest control. Use 'say-as' for a phonetic-spelling rewrite that English-speaking voices read correctly. Use 'espeak' for direct espeak-phonemizer notation.",
  "_status": "v1 — seed entries 2026-05-08. Don adds entries as he hears Kokoro mispronounce terms during review.",
